--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TwoFactorAuthPage.tsx is a thin promotion wrapper: it sets a PageContainer
(title, subtitle, copyLink) and embeds <TOTPEnrollmentSection /> verbatim, so
per-user TOTP enrollment (TOTP enroll/verify, QR + manual secret, backup codes,
regenerate, disable) lives at /account/2fa with a real page title/breadcrumb
under the new "Account" side-nav category instead of competing as a section in
the dense Settings page. The page itself declares no data of its own (the parity
manifest records zero dataSources, zero panels, and exactly two strings —
requiredCount=2: account.twoFactor.title + account.twoFactor.subtitle); the
embedded TOTPEnrollmentSection owns the cache-then-network status feed
(useTOTPStatus) and the four mutations (useTOTPEnroll / useTOTPVerify /
useTOTPRevoke / useTOTPRegenerateBackupCodes) plus its full dialog flow.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 TOTPEnrollmentSection feature-view already exists
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.totpenrollmentsection.TOTPEnrollmentSection)
and owns every TOTP data state for its cache-then-network status feed: the
loading spinner row, the open-mode "requires forward-auth" empty notice, the
not-enrolled body with the Enroll button, the active-credential body
(last-used + backup-codes-remaining + Regenerate/Disable), the stale/offline
notice + retry, the hard-error QueryError + retry, the enroll modal (QR +
manual secret + CopyButton + 6-digit verify + per-error text), the
backup-codes reveal modal (download via SAF + copy), the typed-confirmation
("DISABLE") disable dialog, and the toast queue. This page is its host: it sets
the PageContainer-equivalent header and embeds the feature view — never
re-implementing it (DRY, ADR-006). This mirrors the sibling
notifications/ChannelsPage and notifications/ArchivedPage 2-string wrappers
that embed a shared feature view.

ViewModel note (output spec "@Composable screen + ViewModel"): a thin wrapper
page with zero data sources owns no page-level data, so — exactly like the
shipped ChannelsPage / ArchivedPage / TeslaRegionPage siblings — it does NOT
fabricate an empty page-level ViewModel (that would be a no-op stub, ADR-011).
The real ViewModel exposing the page's StateFlow state is the embedded feature
view's TOTPEnrollmentSectionViewModel (status: StateFlow<UiState<TOTPStatus>>,
dialog: StateFlow<TOTPDialogUiState>), constructed by the feature view from the
host-supplied source. Honest disclosure (no scope narrowing): the manifest's
2 parity items are both strings; there is genuinely no page-owned feed to hoist.

New files (package io.teslasync.android.settings.twofactor):
  - TwoFactorAuthPageModel.kt  Registration(ROUTE_ID account2fa,
                               WEB_PATH /account/2fa, SLUG TwoFactorAuthPage) +
                               recordTwoFactorAuthPageOpened (the one PII-safe
                               view.opened diagnostic, P1/S11). No page-level
                               feed — the embedded feature view owns the TOTP
                               status data.
  - TwoFactorAuthPage.kt       Stateful entry TwoFactorAuthPage(source, logger):
                               records view.opened, renders header above the
                               shared TOTPEnrollmentSection(source, logger);
                               stateless TwoFactorAuthPageContent (verticalScroll
                               Column: header + TOTPEnrollmentSection) +
                               TwoFactorAuthPageHeader (PageTitle + subtitle
                               BodyText + copy-link IconButton writing WEB_PATH
                               to the clipboard).
  - TwoFactorAuthPageHost.kt   TwoFactorAuthRoute() resolves LocalDataContainer,
                               builds the feature view source over
                               HttpTOTPRepository (shared resilient client +
                               offline cache) via bindTOTPEnrollmentSectionSource
                               (repository=…); TwoFactorAuthPageHost.register() ->
                               PageHosts.register("account2fa"). Idempotent.
                               Repository binding (not the shared S8 store) so the
                               feature view's view-model controls refetch-on-retry
                               (refreshTrigger re-collects source.status()); the
                               repo evicts the status cache key on every mutation
                               success (web invalidate(totpKeys.status)).

